Ghidra emitted `(*fist_icall_far(DAT_1000_c6c8))()` with NO args, so 294d received uninitialised __allregs
register slots (param_1=0x9b3d, param_4=0x6e26 in the crash) instead of the asm's ax=0x1358/bx=0x7c3e.
294d does `FUN_0000_260c(param_1,param_4,...)` to resolve the sprite record; a garbage id resolves to a wild
m_260c_recoff, and 298a's `param_3 = g_mem+(recseg<<4)+recoff` lands off g_mem -> wild deref.

FIX (identical to patch 190 for the SAME c6c8=294d method: 294d param_1<-ax, param_4<-bx -- also patch 136's
6c4c REVIEW dispatch and the 294d contract "ax=sprite-directory byte offset; bx=position descriptor").
Thread the two literal register values into the indirect call.  294d uses only param_1 and param_4
(FUN_0000_260c(param_1,param_4,c724)); the other slots are don't-cares (pass 0), matching patch 190's
5-arg cast (uint,uint,uint,uint,uint).

